Yes. Apply that to the target repo. T3 diagnosis complete:

Root cause: QuerySet.values()/values_list() set `_iterable_class` (and `_fields`) on the QuerySet, not on the Query. When a pickled `queryset.query` is assigned to a fresh queryset (`qs2.query = pickle.loads(...)`), the setter just stores `_query` and the fresh queryset keeps `ModelIterable`, so iterating yields model instances built from the values()-shaped select columns → broken instances (pk missing → AttributeError 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'attname').

Fix: in the `query` setter, if the incoming query has `values_select`, switch `_iterable_class` to `ValuesIterable`.

